  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_022) is a minimal RNA-only baseline (pca_n2000, singleprofile, no aggregation) achieving ~48.5% accuracy. The largest unresolved uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit at all. Config_002 is the cleanest test of this question: it keeps the RNA encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (singleprofile), and aggregation (None) identical to config_022, and introduces only the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of adding image information. If accuracy improves substantially, it justifies further investment in multimodal designs and lets us then probe encoder choice, fusion strategy, and profile/aggregation settings. If it does not improve, it strongly suggests the image modality (at least with this RNA representation) is not contributing, redirecting the budget toward RNA-encoder or profile-setting experiments. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental modality question before exploring more complex interactions is the highest-information next step."
}

